ve"},{"id":"c6eadaed-56e7-418b-813c-dd7ceea6cab4","at":"2026-06-12T08:55:28.508Z","channel":"product","event":"signup","actor":{"name":"Aisha","address":"aisha@quartzcollective.test","side":"customer"}},{"id":"b2e5da0f-b912-423c-b208-a86cf3e7fb22","at":"2026-06-12T08:55:28.508Z","channel":"billing","plan":"starter","status":"active","canceledAt":null}],"decisions":[{"id":"989843ef-fbca-4366-8d1d-e0614d675537","kind":"scheduled","evaluatedAt":"2026-06-19T00:00:00.000Z","rawP":0.25,"calibratedP":0.31129026642487007,"calibratedSource":"stored","rationale":"6 days in, no first project and no key milestone despite onboarding email [email:66093a52] and a held welcome call [calendar:a6b650d6]. One invite sent shows some intent, but zero product traction and no inbound questions or tickets after the call suggest low momentum in the remaining 8 days on Starter.","draft":{"from":"nadia@wrenfield.test","to":"aisha@quartzcollective.test","subject":"Getting Quartz Collective's first project going","body":"Hi Aisha,\n\nThanks for making time for the welcome call last week. I saw you've already sent a teammate invite, which is a good start.\n\nThe next step is usually the quickest win: projects are the main organizing unit, and tasks live inside them, and the in-app onboarding flow walks through creating a first project. Once one project exists, the rest tends to fall into place.\n\nWould a short call this week help? I'm happy to walk through setting up that first project with you and answer anything that comes up along the way.\n\nBest,\nNadia"},"actionId":"1d3401f3-041d-44a5-a606-5a36302b680b","evidenceRefs":["ec87d068-7a49-4b26-acff-a24461e2f78f","b2e5da0f-b912-423c-b208-a86cf3e7fb22","8a386435-7f54-4bf0-a805-e85b97c538d8","ebc3ca30-06d6-45a6-9c9a-b92625eab88b","1486e265-9575-4cb6-89bf-550deef5ed18"],"refs":{"email:66093a52":"ebc3ca30-06d6-45a6-9c9a-b92625eab88b","calendar:a6b650d6":"1486e265-9575-4cb6-89bf-550deef5ed18"},"flags":[],"modelId":"claude-opus-5","promptVersion":"dr